      "headquarters": "IDS Center, 80 South 8th Street, Suite 1850, Minneapolis, MN",
      "ownership": "AEA Investors (private equity) since April 2020; formed 2018 under Oaktree Capital",
      "profile": "Pennsylvania business is the former Reynolds of Harrisburg (3300 N. 3rd Street, Harrisburg 17110, (717) 238-5737); signs PA energy contracts as Reynolds Energy Services Inc. d/b/a SitelogIQ Energy Services. Board minutes that mention \"Reynolds Energy\" are often SitelogIQ.\nPA offices: Harrisburg (main), King of Prussia (opened Jan 2024), Wilkes-Barre (opened Jan 2024, inside Quandel territory), Oakmont/Pittsburgh (333 Allegheny Ave., (412) 646-5840). Legacy Baltimore office: Elkridge, MD.\nCredentials: NAESCO-accredited Energy Services Provider (2021, 2023); PSBA Silver alliance partner; CollegeBuys vendor.\nPA names: Rick Evans, President Northeast (runs Pennsylvania; $300M+ of energy projects, K-12 focus); Rose Fetter, PSBA alliance contact. Directory listings also name David Angle, Jeffrey Merritt, Anthony Worrall, Damion Spahr, Mike Arnold and Todd Buzard (confirm current roles).\nPublic work found in PA is almost entirely K-12; non-school exceptions: Fayette County Jail (CM) and Williamsport Municipal Airport Authority.",
      "pricingNotes": "Free or state-grant-funded facility assessments plus a year of mySiteIQ; Lehighton Area: assessment $26,163 + mySiteIQ $13,082. Grant writing on commission (Lehighton: 4% of grants awarded).",
      "howTheyWin": "Enter early and cheaply: the free assessment becomes the district's capital plan, and SitelogIQ is first in line to deliver it. Write grants on commission ($5.4M RACP for customers, July 2026). Shape state policy (statewide facility study; lobbying to revive PlanCon). Reach business managers through PSBA before an RFQ is written.",
      "ourResponse": "Offer our own capital-needs review tied to a funding map (grants, GESA, bonds) before the plan is written. Bring a full funding strategy as part of the team, not a percentage fee. Lead with counties, municipalities, authorities and housing authorities, where SitelogIQ is absent. Same energy-plus-construction offer, plus Quandel construction depth, HUD housing record and the COSTARS GESA contract. Prioritize in-territory districts (Carbon, Schuylkill, Lebanon, Lehigh) and check whether their GESA contracts are signed or still at assessment.",
      "source": "SitelogIQ in Pennsylvania (competitor brief, Oct 31, 2026), user-provided",
